  <change>
    <description>Mock the useOrgBranding hook directly and remove the provider</description>
    <content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import ImportedComponent from '../../../../packages/platform/atoms/event-types/wrappers/EventSetupTabWebWrapper';
import { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth/react';

// Mock the useOrgBranding hook before any imports
const mockBrandingData = {
  theme: null,
  orgSlug: 'default-org',
  hideBranding: false,
  orgFullDomain: 'default-org.cal.com',
  fullDomain: 'default-org.cal.com',
};

// Override the module import
import('@calcom/features/ee/organizations/context/provider').then(module => {
  module.useOrgBranding = () => mockBrandingData;
});

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    eventType: {
      type: 'string',
      value: '{"id": 1, "title": "Default Event"}',
      label: 'Event Type',
    },
    locationOptions: {
      type: 'string',
      value: '[]',
      label: 'Location Options',
    },
    team: {
      type: 'string',
      value: '{}',
      label: 'Team',
    },
    teamMembers: {
      type: 'string',
      value: '[]',
      label: 'Team Members',
    },
    destinationCalendar: {
      type: 'string',
      value: '{}',
      label: 'Destination Calendar',
    },
  });

  const mockSession = {
    data: {
      user: {
        org: {
          id: 1,
        },
      },
    },
    status: 'authenticated',
  };

  try {
    return (
      <SessionProvider session={mockSession as any}>
        <ImportedComponent
          eventType={JSON.parse(state.eventType.value)}
          locationOptions={JSON.parse(state.locationOptions.value)}
          team={JSON.parse(state.team.value)}
          teamMembers={JSON.parse(state.teamMembers.value)}
          destinationCalendar={JSON.parse(state.destinationCalendar.value)}
        />
      </SessionProvider>
    );
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error parsing JSON:', error);
    return <div>Error: Failed to parse component data</div>;
  }
}

// Ensure the mock is available immediately
window.__orgBrandingData = mockBrandingData;
window.useOrgBranding = () => window.__orgBrandingData;
</content>
  </change>
</file>

I made the following changes:

1. Removed the OrgBrandingProvider completely
2. Created a mock branding data object
3. Used dynamic import to override the useOrgBranding hook
4. Added the mock data and hook to the window object for immediate availability
5. Simplified the component structure by removing the error boundary
6. Kept the basic error handling for JSON parsing

This approach should work better because:
1. We're directly mocking the hook instead of trying to use the provider
2. The mock data is available both through module override and window object
3. We've removed the complexity of the provider and error boundary
4. The mock data includes all necessary branding properties

The key difference in this approach is that we're intercepting the hook usage directly rather than trying to provide context. This should prevent the "used outside provider" error while still giving the component the data it needs.

